# SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000080  -  CAT II
# The web server must provide install options to exclude installation of
# utility programs, services, plug-ins, and modules not necessary for
# operation.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000080
group:           V-206379
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000381
control_rev5:    CM-7

contribution:    Every utility, plug-in, and module Splunk adds beyond the core daemon
                 arrives as an app or as an optional process, and the application can set
                 each app's state explicitly, record whether the app permits being
                 disabled, and switch off the optional KV Store process.

governs:         app.conf - Settings for an installed app: whether it is enabled, visible, and what it
                 may do.
governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.

check:           app.conf [install] state present
check:           app.conf [install] allows_disable present
check:           server.conf [kvstore] disabled present

external:        The installer's option set and uninstall facility, which are properties of
                 the distributed package rather than of the running configuration.
external:        Utility programs present on the host outside the application, carried by
                 the operating system build.
external:        Which app-supplied utilities the deployment genuinely needs, carried by
                 the app review procedure.

citation:        Web Server SRG SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000080 check and fix text;
                 app.conf.spec:124 (state), app.conf.spec:154 (allows_disable, default
                 true), server.conf.spec:5234 (kvstore disabled)
finding:         Installed apps carry no declared state or disable property, or the
                 optional KV Store process is left at its default, so the application does
                 not show that only the utilities and modules needed for operation are
                 present and active.
